  "tasks": [
    {
      "template": "fix-bug",
      "vars": {
        "report": "online, glimmers keep losing health to shots fired at them from behind the pillars, and a player with a modified client scores hits on anyone, anywhere in the pit"
      },
      "edits": [
        {
          "file": "scripts/arena_match.gd",
          "find": "\tif claim != shot.target:\n\t\t# The client saw it otherwise (it draws others a little in the past, or it lies): the server's trace stands.\n\t\trefused_claims += 1\n",
          "replace": "\tif claim != shot.target:\n\t\trefused_claims += 1\n\t\tif claim >= 0 and claim != slot:\n\t\t\t# The client saw the hit first: take its word, so a hit lands the moment the player sees it.\n\t\t\tshot.target = claim\n"
        }
      ],
      "hidden": [
        "hidden/test_hidden_claims.gd"
      ],
      "reference": "solutions/prototype/fix-bug",
      "decoy": "solutions/prototype/fix-bug-decoy"
    },
    {
      "template": "write-tests",
      "vars": {
        "subject": "match rules (scripts/arena_match.gd with the movement and shots of scripts/sim.gd and the pillars of scripts/court.gd)",
        "file": "test/unit/test_match_rules.gd",
        "rules": "a shot that reaches a glimmer takes one health, a pillar stops a shot, a glimmer cannot fire again until its cooldown has run, the hit that takes the last health knocks the glimmer out of the round, the last glimmer standing wins the round and scores a point, a slot that reaches the target score wins the match, and a pillar stops a glimmer that walks into it",
        "code": "scripts/arena_match.gd, scripts/sim.gd or scripts/court.gd"
      },
      "unchanged": [
        "scripts/arena_match.gd",
        "scripts/sim.gd",
        "scripts/court.gd"
      ],
      "mutantTests": [
        "test/unit/test_match_rules.gd"
      ],
      "mutants": [
        {
          "file": "scripts/arena_match.gd",
          "find": "\tf.hp -= DAMAGE\n",
          "replace": "\tf.hp -= 0\n",
          "name": "a hit takes no health"
        },
        {
          "file": "scripts/arena_match.gd",
          "find": "\tif f.hp <= 0:\n",
          "replace": "\tif f.hp < 0:\n",
          "name": "the last hit does not knock the glimmer out"
        },
        {
          "file": "scripts/arena_match.gd",
          "find": "\tif alive.size() <= 1:\n",
          "replace": "\tif alive.size() < 1:\n",
          "name": "the last one standing does not end the round"
        },
        {
          "file": "scripts/arena_match.gd",
          "find": "\t\tscores[round_winner] += 1\n",
          "replace": "\t\tscores[round_winner] += 0\n",
          "name": "the round winner scores nothing"
        },
        {
          "file": "scripts/arena_match.gd",
          "find": "scores[round_winner] >= TARGET:",
          "replace": "scores[round_winner] > TARGET:",
          "name": "the target score does not end the match"
        },
        {
          "file": "scripts/sim.gd",
          "find": "\tvar reach := court.ray_length(origin, dir, RANGE)\n",
          "replace": "\tvar reach := RANGE\n",
          "name": "shots pass through pillars"
        },
        {
          "file": "scripts/sim.gd",
          "find": "\tif bool(input.fire) and f.cooldown == 0:\n",
          "replace": "\tif bool(input.fire):\n",
          "name": "the cooldown does not hold a shot"
        },
        {
          "file": "scripts/court.gd",
          "find": "\t\tx = wall.position.x - HALF if dx > 0 else wall.end.x + HALF\n",
          "replace": "\t\tx = x\n",
          "name": "glimmers walk through pillars sideways"
        }
      ],
      "reference": "solutions/prototype/write-tests"
    },
    {
      "template": "add-feature",
      "vars": {
        "feature": "a dash. An input with \"dash\" true makes the glimmer move at three times its speed for 5 ticks, the tick of the press included, and it cannot dash again until 45 ticks after the press (a press during either is ignored). Sim.step does it from the input's \"dash\" key, so the server and a client's prediction move alike; the Fighter keeps its dash state, which travels in snapshots (Fighter.to_array and from_array), and the server keeps \"dash\" when it cleans an input (Sim.sanitize). ArenaClient.step takes it as a sixth argument dash (false by default) and sends it, so a dash online needs no correction"
      },
      "hidden": [
        "hidden/test_hidden_dash.gd"
      ],
      "reference": "solutions/prototype/add-feature"
    },
